        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(line): AI-assisted - requireMention can now optionally gate non-text messages with bounded pending-media retention",
        "body": "Closes #103758\n\n<details>\n<summary>Additional instructions</summary>\n\n**MUST:** Keep **Allow edits from maintainers** enabled for this PR so maintainers\ncan help update the branch when needed.\n\n</details>\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where LINE groups configured with `requireMention: true` could not require a mention before non-text messages (image/video/audio/file) reached the agent. Any photo, video, voice clip, or file posted in such a group was always processed, regardless of whether the bot was actually mentioned, because LINE's Messaging API never attaches mention metadata to non-text messages and the mention-gate logic could not account for that.\n\nFixes an issue where operators of mention-gated LINE groups would see the bot react to every image/video/audio/file dropped in the chat, even when nobody addressed the bot, when they expected the same \"must be mentioned\" behavior that already applies to text messages (per #34438 / #35847).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds two new **opt-in** LINE group config fields — `requireMentionForNonText` and `pendingMediaLimit` — so operators can explicitly turn on mention gating for non-text messages without changing default behavior for anyone else. Because LINE never reports a mention on the non-text message itself, a bounded per-group pending-media queue (default limit 3) retains the most recent skipped media until a later message in the same group is mentioned and fully processed, at which point the queued media is attached to that turn and the queue is cleared. This lets a user post a photo, then follow up with `@bot look at this`, and have the photo still reach the agent.\n\nA prior attempt at the opt-in flag alone (#68197) went stale without merging and did not include the retention queue, which meant skipped media was simply dropped forever once a group opted in — this PR keeps the same opt-in, default-false posture that maintainers asked for on #68197, and adds the missing retention piece on top.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLINE operators can now set `channels.line.accounts.<id>.groups.<groupId>.requireMentionForNonText: true` (alongside `requireMention: true`) to require an `@mention` before non-text messages reach the agent, matching the existing text-message behavior. Skipped media isn't lost — up to `pendingMediaLimit` (default 3) recent items are retained per group and delivered alongside the next mentioned message. Existing configs are unaffected since both fields default to off/unset.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`pnpm test:extension line` — 26 test files, **313 tests passing** (up from 307 on `main`; +6 in `bot-handlers.test.ts`, +2 in `config-schema.test.ts`):\n\n```\n Test Files  26 passed (26)\n      Tests  313 passed (313)\n```\n\nNew tests cover:\n\n- unmentioned non-text message is skipped when `requireMentionForNonText` is set (and the pre-existing \"allows non-text through by default\" test is preserved unchanged, proving no default-behavior change);\n- pending-queue eviction bounded by `pendingMediaLimit` (oldest dropped first);\n- queued media flushed into `allMedia`/`processMessage` context on a later mentioned message, then the queue is cleared;\n- default `pendingMediaLimit` of 3 when unset;\n- schema acceptance of both new fields and rejection of non-positive `pendingMediaLimit`.\n\nAdditional local validation:\n\n- `npx tsc -p extensions/line/tsconfig.json --noEmit` — clean, exit 0\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/line` — 0 warnings/errors\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-config-doc-baseline.ts --check` — passes after regenerating `docs/.generated/config-baseline.sha256` for the new config surface\n- `node scripts/format-docs.mjs --check` / `markdownlint-cli2` / `node scripts/check-docs-mdx.mjs` — all clean on `docs/channels/line.md`\n- `codex` CLI was not available in this environment, so `codex review --base origin/main` could not be run locally; noting this per CONTRIBUTING.md instead of skipping silently.\n\n---\n\n### AI-assisted PR\n\n- [x] Mark as AI-assisted in the PR title or description — this PR was authored by an AI coding agent (Claude, via OpenClaw) under human supervision.\n- [x] Evidence section above includes the most useful validation (test run, typecheck, lint, docs checks).\n- [ ] Prompts/session logs not attached in this submission.\n- [x] Confirm you understand what the code does — implementation and tests were reviewed line-by-line before submission.\n- [ ] `codex review --base origin/main` not run — `codex` CLI is not installed in this environment (noted above).\n- [x] Will resolve/reply to bot review conversations addressed during review.\n",
        "branch": "fix/line-pending-media-queue",
